<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The mechanite dressing's cast job: VEF's VFEA_GotoTargetAndUseAbility with the driver swapped
    for MedicWarcasket.JobDriver_MechaniteDressing, which walks to the patient without ordering
    them to stand (see its header). reportString is never shown, the driver reports the
    ability's jobReportString, but it is a translatable field the walker lists.

    checkOverrideOnDamage Never: damage never interrupts the job in any phase. Vanilla considers
    an override only for a job that is not player-forced, and the dressing is not always
    player-forced (a queued order, a drafted pilot's cast), so the def says it outright.

    neverShowWeapon: the pilot holsters the weapon for the whole job, walk included, as vanilla's
    touch abilities (CastAbilityTouch) do. PawnRenderUtility.DrawEquipmentAndApparelExtras
    reads it before both the aimed and the carried draw, and it outranks a drafted pilot or a
    raid lord's AlwaysShowWeapon; worn apparel still draws.
  -->
  <JobDef>
    <defName>MDWC_MechaniteDressing</defName>
    <driverClass>MedicWarcasket.JobDriver_MechaniteDressing</driverClass>
    <reportString>dressing TargetA's wounds.</reportString>
    <checkOverrideOnDamage>Never</checkOverrideOnDamage>
    <neverShowWeapon>true</neverShowWeapon>
    <carryThingAfterJob>true</carryThingAfterJob>
  </JobDef>
</Defs>
